atures and global frequency domain information. This is achieved through a two-pronged approach, using three significant modules: DWT-Based Local Spatial-Frequency Domain Feature Capture Block (LoSFB), FFT-Based Global Frequency Domain Feature Capture Block (GloFB), and a Window Attention Block (WAttention).\n\n  1. Data Transformation and Feature Extraction:\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nA Review of TRiSM Frameworks in Artificial Intelligence Systems: Fundamentals, Taxonomy, Use Cases, Key Challenges and Future Directions - Ray - 2026 - Expert Systems - Wiley Online Library (https://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/10.1111/exsy.70213)\nciteturn4search5 [wordlim: 200] Published: 7 months ago; Crawled: last week; “ Purge Profanity: An AI System to Detect Profanity/Obscenity From Texts and Images.” ... “Provenance Detection for AI-Generated Images: Combining Perceptual Hashing, Homomorphic Encryption, and AI Detection Models.” ... “Reputational Risk Associated With Big Data Research and Development: An Interdisciplinary Perspective.”\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nPrompt-based Distribution Alignment (PDA) (https://api.emergentmind.com/topics/prompt-based-distribution-alignment-pda)\nciteturn4search6 [wordlim: 200] Published: 10 months ago; Crawled: 2 months ago; LLM Attribute/Value Alignment  | ALIGN (Ravichandran et al., 11 Jul 2025)  | +10-25% accuracy for survey/value alignment, instant personalization by prompt selectionPost-hoc OOD Detection  | PDA-KNN (Wang et al., 15 Feb 2025)  | 96.73% average accuracy, +16.07% vs. baseline for novel generative methods ...   * Attribute-conditioned Distribution Matching (ALIGN):\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nPDA: Generalizable Detection of AI-Generated Images via Post-hoc Distribution Alignment | Cool Papers - Immersive Paper Discovery (https://papers.cool/arxiv/2502.108